{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F45AnIngestingDocumentHoldsOneModel",
    "description": "Finding F45. A document that ingests may hold exactly ONE model. Add a second — a mounted leaf, or an inert model like `Bystander` below — and EVERY assertion in the document errors with `Interpreter build failed: document holds several models; pass model_name`, including assertions that touch no ingested value at all.\n\nWHAT MAKES IT ATTRIBUTABLE, and it is one line. Delete `Bystander` and `Ingest`'s assertion passes at 8, still ingesting. Delete `Ingest`'s `update: {kind: \"data\"}` block instead, leaving two models and no ingest, and the document BUILDS — `Bystander` passes and `Ingest` reports `actual=0 expected=8`, a wrong NUMBER rather than a refusal, because the parameter no longer has a source. `runs/micro_exhaust_run.esm` is the same case done properly, and it is in the tree today: three models, nine assertions, green. Two models is fine. Ingesting is fine. The two together are refused, and the refusal is at interpreter build, after `esm validate` has passed.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS. It is the wall PLAN.md §7's architecture meets. Phase 7 mounts a shared domain document into a thin per-fixture document that configures it and asserts canonical output in its own `tests` section; the fixture's asserting model is the second model, and the mount is the first. Measured in `spikes/7a/`: the mount evaluates correctly and emits the right relation, and the moment an asserting model is added beside it, all of it errors. `--model NAME` does not rescue it — it narrows which tests are REPORTED without reaching the build — and building the asserting model alone (`esm simulate --model Check`) loses the mounted names entirely, `E_TREEWALK_UNBOUND_NAME: 'AgeGroupCensus.totalAge'`. The four `runs/*.esm` assemblies in this tree are green only because none of them ingests.\n\nA SECOND MEASUREMENT, taken at the same time and the same root cause. `pkg/earthsci-ast-rs/src/prepare.rs` picks ONE model and builds it, and the index-set registry it uses is `file.index_sets`, the document's own. So a `subsystems` child is invisible to this path as well: mounted as a `{ref}` stub it is never resolved, and INLINED as a literal model body it still leaves `Census.totalAge` unbound at build while `esm validate` accepts the document. There is no nesting spelling that reaches the ingesting interpreter.\n\nTHIS REPRO. `Ingest` reads one column of one row — runspecmonth.monthID, monthID 8, the smallest table in the corpus, chosen because the point is that ANY ingest is enough. `Bystander` computes 1 + 1. The intended behaviour is that both assertions pass; today both error.\n\nFIX SHAPE. Build every model in the document, as the scalar path already does, and resolve a name across models the way the flattener does — or, more narrowly, let the ingesting build take the union of the document's models when no `model_name` is given, which is the behaviour a document with one model already gets.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "finding", "repro"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
    "f45_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_f45_runspecmonth" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["runspec"], "esio_format": "parquet", "note": "One row, monthID 8." }
    }
  },

  "metaparameters": {
    "n_f45_runspecmonth": {
      "type": "integer", "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecmonth, discovered by the source's own extent. 1."
    }
  },

  "index_sets": {
    "f45_month_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": "n_f45_runspecmonth" }
  },

  "models": {
    "Ingest": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },
      "variables": {
        "rsm_monthID": {
          "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "shape": ["f45_month_rows"],
          "description": "runspecmonth.monthID. 8.",
          "update": { "kind": "data", "source": "f45_runspecmonth", "from": { "file_variable": "monthID" } }
        },
        "monthTotal": {
          "type": "unknown", "units": "1",
          "description": "8, lifted onto a scalar because a kind: data parameter is not assertable (finding F43)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "monthTotal",
          "rhs": { "op": "aggregate", "args": [], "semiring": "sum_product", "output_idx": [],
            "ranges": { "m": { "from": "f45_month_rows" } },
            "expr": { "op": "index", "args": ["rsm_monthID", "m"] } }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_ingested_value_is_readable",
          "description": "8. Passes the moment `Bystander` is deleted from this file, which is what attributes the failure to the model COUNT and not to the ingest.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "monthTotal", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.0 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "Bystander": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },
      "variables": {
        "two": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "2. Touches no data and no other model." }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "two",
          "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": [
            { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0 },
            { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0 }
          ] }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "arithmetic_that_touches_no_data_still_fails",
          "description": "1 + 1. This model neither ingests nor names anything outside itself, and its assertion errors for the same reason the one above does: the DOCUMENT ingests, so the whole build is refused.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "two", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.0 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
